*> Test of 30 part 8 section 5, Calibrated sculk sensor (core/src/redstone-30-8.cob; T0826): radius and ticks, the back input, the frequency filter and the output side.
*> A case loads its inputs from a text of numbers (LOAD-IN fills WS-I as integers and WS-FX as doubles), calls the program
*> and shows the outputs WS-R(1..WS-N) joined by "/", one group per call; expected values come from the rules and tables of the section.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-REDSTONE-30-8-5.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY INTERACT.
 01 WS-ISG.
    05 WS-I1 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-I2 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-I3 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-I4 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-I5 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-I6 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-I7 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-I8 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-I9 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-I10 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-I11 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-I12 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-I13 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-I14 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-I15 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-I16 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-IST REDEFINES WS-ISG.
    05 WS-I BINARY-LONG OCCURS 16 TIMES.
 01 WS-FXSG.
    05 WS-FX1 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-FX2 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-FX3 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-FX4 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-FX5 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-FX6 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-FX7 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-FX8 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-FX9 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-FX10 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-FX11 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-FX12 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-FX13 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-FX14 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-FX15 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-FX16 FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-FXST REDEFINES WS-FXSG.
    05 WS-FX FLOAT-LONG OCCURS 16 TIMES.
 01 WS-RSG.
    05 WS-R1 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-R2 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-R3 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-R4 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-R5 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-R6 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-R7 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-R8 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-R9 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-R10 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-R11 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-R12 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-R13 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-R14 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-R15 BINARY-LONG.
    05 WS-R16 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-RST REDEFINES WS-RSG.
    05 WS-R BINARY-LONG OCCURS 16 TIMES.
 01 WS-RFSG.
    05 WS-RF1 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-RF2 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-RF3 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-RF4 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-RF5 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-RF6 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-RF7 FLOAT-LONG.
    05 WS-RF8 FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-RFST REDEFINES WS-RFSG.
    05 WS-RF FLOAT-LONG OCCURS 8 TIMES.
 01 WS-IN                  PIC X(160).
 01 WS-TOK                 PIC X(24).
 01 WS-P                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-K                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-N                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-J                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PTR                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SHOW                PIC -(10)9.
 01 WS-TEXTS.
    05 WS-T1               PIC X(96).
    05 WS-T2               PIC X(96).
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "acceptance US12 30-8§5 Calibrated sculk sensor: constants (5, 4.1): listener radius 8 (calibrated 16), active ticks 30 (calibrated 10), cooldown 10 (calibrated, radius, active ticks, cooldown)" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM BEGIN-CASE
     MOVE "0" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-SENSOR-CONST" USING WS-I1 WS-R1 WS-R2 WS-R3
     MOVE 3 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-SENSOR-CONST" USING WS-I1 WS-R1 WS-R2 WS-R3
     MOVE 3 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "8/30/10 16/10/10" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance US12 30-8§5 Calibrated sculk sensor: back side (5): the signal is read from pos.relative(opp(facing)), the side toward the placer (facing data value; back direction)" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM BEGIN-CASE
     MOVE "2" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-BACK" USING WS-I1 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "3" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-BACK" USING WS-I1 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "4" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-BACK" USING WS-I1 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "5" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-BACK" USING WS-I1 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "3 2 5 4" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance US12 30-8§5 Calibrated sculk sensor: canReceiveVibration (5): with back = 0 every non-zero frequency is accepted; with back = n only events of frequency n; the plain sensor rule still" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM BEGIN-CASE
     MOVE "0 1 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-CAN-RECEIVE" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "0 15 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-CAN-RECEIVE" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "6 6 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-CAN-RECEIVE" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "6 5 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-CAN-RECEIVE" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "6 10 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-CAN-RECEIVE" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "6 1 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-CAN-RECEIVE" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "0 0 0" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-CAN-RECEIVE" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "6 6 0" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-CAN-RECEIVE" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "1 1 1 0 0 0 0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance US12 30-8§5 Calibrated sculk sensor: output side (5, V13): getSignal is 0 when the direction equals facing (the back receives nothing), else the power; getDirectSignal is inherited," TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM BEGIN-CASE
     MOVE "8 2 2 0" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-SIGNAL" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-I4 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "8 2 3 0" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-SIGNAL" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-I4 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "8 2 5 0" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-SIGNAL" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-I4 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "8 2 1 0" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-SIGNAL" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-I4 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "8 2 1 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-SIGNAL" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-I4 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "8 2 2 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-SIGNAL" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-I4 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "8 2 0 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-SIGNAL" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-I4 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "0 8 8 8 8 0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance US12 30-8§5 Calibrated sculk sensor: radius 16 strength (5, V3): distance 0 or 1 gives 15, 4 gives 12, 8 gives 8, 16 gives 1 (radius, distance squared)" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM BEGIN-CASE
     MOVE "16 0" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-STRENGTH" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "16 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-STRENGTH" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "16 16" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-STRENGTH" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "16 64" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-STRENGTH" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "16 256" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-STRENGTH" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "15 15 12 8 1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "acceptance US12 30-8§5 Calibrated sculk sensor: worked example 11.2 (11): calibrated sensor facing south, a repeater behind it outputs 6: shear (6), entity_mount (6) and entity_interact (6)" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM BEGIN-CASE
     MOVE "6 6 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-CAN-RECEIVE" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "6 6 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-CAN-RECEIVE" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "6 6 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-CAN-RECEIVE" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "6 1 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-CAN-RECEIVE" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "6 10 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-CAN-RECEIVE" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "0 1 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-CAN-RECEIVE" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "0 10 1" TO WS-IN
     PERFORM LOAD-IN
     CALL "RS3-CAL-CAN-RECEIVE" USING WS-I1 WS-I2 WS-I3 WS-R1
     MOVE 1 TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-N
     MOVE "1 1 1 0 0 1 1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.

 BEGIN-CASE.
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR
     .

 LOAD-IN.
     MOVE 1 TO WS-P
     PERFORM VARYING WS-K FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-K > 16
         MOVE SPACES TO WS-TOK
         IF WS-P <= 160
             UNSTRING WS-IN DELIMITED BY ALL SPACE INTO WS-TOK WITH POINTER WS-P
         END-IF
         COMPUTE WS-FX(WS-K) = FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-TOK)
         COMPUTE WS-I(WS-K) = FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-TOK)
     END-PERFORM
     .

 ADD-N.
     PERFORM VARYING WS-J FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-J > WS-N
         MOVE WS-R(WS-J) TO WS-SHOW
         IF WS-J > 1
             STRING "/" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
         END-IF
         STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHOW) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     END-PERFORM
     STRING " " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     .

 ADD-TEXT.
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-T1) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-T2) " " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     .
 END PROGRAM TEST-REDSTONE-30-8-5.
